  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nAn upper level low off the Pac NW coast today will continue it's \ngradual SE trajectory. Light rain showers across northern portion\nof Humboldt County this afternoon will expand slightly south and \neast late this evening and overnight, with light rain shower \nactivity reaching most of Humboldt County and NW portions of Elko\nCounty. Winds this afternoon will be breezy once again, with \nslightly higher winds expected across central NV. Winds across \neast-central NV approach low end advisory levels Friday afternoon,\nwith sustained SW winds of 15 to 25 mph and gust to 45 mph in \nvalley locations across White Pine County, with higher terrain \nlikely reaching advisory level gusts. Dry across the CWA on \nSaturday. Sunday scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms are\nexpected across mainly the eastern half of the CWA, and possibly\nthe NW corner of Humboldt County. Periods of unsettled weather\ncontinue into early next week. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in below normal\ntemperatures and moderate confidence in precipitation chances for\nthe next several days. Increasing confidence regarding storms this\nweekend, currently sitting around the moderate level. No changes\nto NBM output.",
